DEF wPaletteBufBg EQU $D800 ; bank W7 size 64 array CONFIRMED [ramop7] staging buffer of the 8 background palettes (8 bytes each: 4 colors of 2 bytes, RGB555): filled by Palette_LoadToBuffer (4F:4000: DE = destination in bank 7, HL = source in ROM bank A, BC = byte count) and written to the hardware by Palette_UploadBuffer (4F:404B: 8 palettes from [HL] through BCPS/BCPD; executed in 63 of the 64 scenarios of analysis/coverage_union.tsv, and only under bank 7 in the 41 bank-observed replays of analysis/rambank/observed_banks.tsv)
DEF wPaletteBufObj EQU $D840 ; bank W7 size 64 array CONFIRMED [ramop7] staging buffer of the 8 object palettes, the 64 bytes after wPaletteBufBg: Palette_UploadBuffer (4F:404B) reads them from [HL + $40] and writes them through OCPS/OCPD; Palette_LoadToBuffer copies BC bytes into it (8 to 64: 51 of its 76 object destinations copy a whole 64-byte half, the others single palettes or a few: DE = wPaletteBufObj + 8 * n)
DEF wSpriteSlotBackup EQU $D900 ; bank W3 size 256 array CONFIRMED [ramop7] WRAM bank 3 backup of the sprite slot page: Sprites_SaveSlotsToBank3 (7F:624F) copies the 256 bytes $DA00-$DAFF of bank 7 (the 14 slots of 16 bytes and the 32 bytes after them) here byte by byte, switching between banks 7 and 3 for every byte, and Sprites_RestoreSlotsFromBank3 (7F:627C) copies them back; observed in 7 of the bank-observed replays (7F:624F-62A8: bank 7 only between the bank 7 idiom and the push, bank 3 only after the bank 3 idiom)
DEF wScreenTileMap EQU $D000 ; bank W7 size 1024 array CONFIRMED [ramop8] the screen buffer of tile numbers: 32 x 32 bytes, row stride $20, the 20 x 18 visible tiles are its top left corner (an offset is $20 * row + column); Tilemap_CopyRectAndAttr (00:08EA, 63 of the 64 scenarios of analysis/coverage_union.tsv) and Tilemap_CopyRectAndAttrPtr (00:16A2) copy rectangles into it (and a second rectangle of attributes $0400 bytes higher), Tilemap_FillRectSequential (48:4679) and Tilemap_FillAscendingWithAttr (4F:45C6) fill it; Gfx_UploadBgMapBuffers (00:082C: 63 of 64 scenarios, only under bank 7 in the 41 bank-observed replays), Gfx_UploadBgMapBuffersDi (00:07CB), ...NoService (00:085B) and Gfx_UploadWinMapBuffers (00:0887) send its first $240 bytes (18 rows, C = $24 blocks of 16) by general-purpose DMA (the project says HDMA: HDMA5 bit 7 = 0) to the map of VRAM bank 0 at $9800 or $9C00, CommScene_UploadBackgroundMap (70:4638) all $400; never executed and without a caller in the tree: Tilemap_ClearBuffers (00:093B, clears both buffers), Tilemap_CopyRectAndAttrSplitSrc (00:08CA), Gfx_UploadWinMapBuffersDi (00:07FB)
DEF wScreenAttrMap EQU $D400 ; bank W7 size 1024 array CONFIRMED [ramop8] the screen buffer of tile attributes: the 1,024 bytes $0400 after wScreenTileMap (the second pass of Tilemap_CopyRectAndAttr works at DE + $0400, Tilemap_FillAscendingWithAttr stores the attribute at H + 4, Tilemap_FillRectSequential fills HL + $0400 through Tilemap_ApplyMaskRect); the same routines send its first $240 bytes (18 rows) by general-purpose DMA to the map of VRAM bank 1 ($9800 or $9C00, E = 1), CommScene_UploadBackgroundMap (70:4638) all $400
